1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:02,268
Your electric bill just jumped.

2
00:00:02,857 --> 00:00:04,387
Everyone blames AI.

3
00:00:04,977 --> 00:00:06,726
But nobody can show you the number.

4
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:09,480
Kilo What? measures it,

5
00:00:09,774 --> 00:00:11,155
on your own computer.

6
00:00:11,155 --> 00:00:13,785
No cloud, no account, no extra hardware.

7
00:00:15,111 --> 00:00:16,686
Every two seconds, it reads

8
00:00:16,686 --> 00:00:18,610
your machine's own power sensors,

9
00:00:18,978 --> 00:00:20,846
finds every AI app running,

10
00:00:21,214 --> 00:00:22,963
and splits the watts between them.

11
00:00:24,289 --> 00:00:27,020
You see it live: watts, pesos and carbon,

12
00:00:27,462 --> 00:00:28,891
in dark mode or light.

13
00:00:30,218 --> 00:00:31,668
Then it forecasts your bill:

14
00:00:32,037 --> 00:00:33,760
pre-trained on the Luzon grid,

15
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:35,599
fine-tuned on your own readings,

16
00:00:35,968 --> 00:00:37,974
and tested on data it never saw.

17
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:42,180
Ask Kilo, an AI that runs on your own machine.

18
00:00:42,696 --> 00:00:44,001
The app does the math;

19
00:00:44,001 --> 00:00:45,662
Kilo puts it in plain words.

20
00:00:47,724 --> 00:00:49,123
On this laptop, AI was

21
00:00:49,123 --> 00:00:50,839
half a percent of the jump.

22
00:00:51,428 --> 00:00:53,032
When it's more, it shows the fix,

23
00:00:53,032 --> 00:00:54,052
and what you'll save.

24
00:00:55,673 --> 00:00:57,700
Kilo What? Measured, not guessed.

